      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was founded in 1863 after gold was discovered in Alder Gulch, quickly becoming Montana's territorial capital from 1865 to 1875.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginia_City%2C_Montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Kids can try gold panning, ride the historic Alder Gulch Shortline Railroad, and experience a stagecoach tour for an interactive gold‑rush lesson.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://roamstates.com/destinations/virginia-city-montana",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Virginia City Players perform at the historic Opera House, the oldest continuously operating summer‑stock theater west of the Mississippi.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://roamstates.com/destinations/virginia-city-montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1961 the Virginia City Historic District was designated a National Historic Landmark District, preserving over 150 authentic gold‑rush buildings.",
